      {
        "title": "The Tailor's Craft at Paul Revere House",
        "description": "<p>Clothing historian Henry Cooke takes on the role of an early Boston tailor. Watch as he “takes the measure” of visitors, then sits cross-legged, fashioning waistcoats from luxurious fabrics and “slops” from coarse weaves.</p>",
