      {
        "title": "Bunker Hill Parade",
        "description": "<h3>Bunker Hill Parade</h3>\n<h4>Sunday, June 15, 12:30 p.m. - 3:30 p.m.</h4>\n<p>The Bunker Hill Parade Committee will host the annual Bunker Hill Parade. The parade commemorates the Battle of Bunker Hill, the armed services, and the essence of American heritage while celebrating the historic neighborhood of Charlestown. The parade begins at the intersection of Vine and Bunker Hill Streets, passes down Main Street and concludes at the Charlestown Militia Training Field. Bunker Hill Grounds and the Massachusetts Gate entry to the grounds are prime viewing areas for the parade, which National Park Service staff march in annually.</p>\n<p>To learn more about other commemorative events, please visit our page <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/articles/000/bh-commemoration-week.htm\">Bunker Hill Commemoration Week 2025</a>.</p>",
        "category": "Special Event",
        "tags": [
          "Boston National Historical Park",
          "boston",
          "american revolution",
          "Battle of Bunker Hill",
          "bunker hill",
          "america250"
        ],
        "location": "The parade will begin at 12:30 p.m. Participants will march from Vine Street to Bunker Hill Street, to Main Street, to Monument Avenue, to Monument Square, to Winthrop Street to Common Street. Streets along the route will be closed to traffic through approximately 5 p.m. For more information, visit: https://bunkerhillparade.com.",
        "coordinates": {
          "latitude": "",
          "longitude": ""
        },
        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      },
      {
        "title": "Concert: Finesse Duo",
        "description": "<p><em>The <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/long/planyourvisit/summer-festival.htm\">Longfellow Summer Arts Festival</a> brings music, poetry, and community to the East Lawn of the Longfellow House on Sunday afternoons through the summer. All events are free and open to the public. This concert is presented in partnership with the <a href=\"https://college.berklee.edu/events/summer\">Berklee Summer in the City</a> concert series.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Finesse</strong> is a vibrant duo made up of Gabriela Joya and Maria Medina, known for their dynamic blend of Latin jazz and Cuban music. Joya, a gifted vocalist and traditional instrument player, began her musical journey in Cuba, where she developed a deep love for the rhythms of her homeland. Medina, a skilled percussionist and pianist, earned her music degrees studying under renowned instructors and refining her craft across genres.</p>\n<p>Together, they create a lively and engaging sound, full of catchy melodies, intricate rhythms, and energetic improvisation. Their performances celebrate the rich traditions of Cuban music while bringing a fresh, modern twist to the Latin jazz scene. Whether in intimate settings or large concert halls, Finesse captivates audiences with their chemistry, musicality, and passion, making them a standout act wherever they perform.</p>",
        "category": "Special Event",
        "tags": [],
        "location": "",
        "coordinates": {
          "latitude": "",
          "longitude": ""
        },
        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      }
    ]
  }
