      "title": "Ranger-Guided Walk: Island Ford Pond and River Ramble",
      "description": "<p>Join the National Park Service for a cool summer walk around Island Ford Pond and into Falling Branch to discover the amazing stream life. Grab your water shoes or closed toe sandals for a splish-splashing good time.  We will conclude by walking along the edge of the river where you might see geese, ducks, a great blue heron fishing in the shallows or maybe a Midland Water Snake.  Wonderful wet excitement awaits.   We might catch a glimpse of an Osprey or a even a Bald Eagle. All youth must be accompanied by an adult.</p>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Location: </strong>1978 Island Ford Parkway; Sandy Springs, Georgia 30350.  We will meet in front of the historic Hewlett lodge.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Facilities:  </strong>Located in the Hewlett Lodge Visitor Center</p>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Difficulty:  </strong>Fairly easy walking on level ground around the pond.  Slippery rocks and mud in and along Falling Branch.  Brief uphill returning to Hewlett Lodge from River.  Note: This walk is not suitable for very young children.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Bring</strong>: Please bring <strong><u>WATER</u></strong>.  Remember to dress for the weather and wear water shoes or closed toe sandals.  <strong><u>NO FLIP-FLOPS ALLOWED!</u></strong> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Limit: </strong>30 persons</p>",
