        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "2025-07-14, 2025-07-21",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      },
      {
        "title": "Canyon Rim Walk",
        "description": "<p>Join a ranger for a hike along one of the short trails near the Visitor Center.  Learn about the history, geology, plants, and animals of the monument.  The hike will be on a fairly level, easy trail and the total distance will not exceed one mile. </p>\n<p>Bring water, sunscreen, snacks, and your questions!  Closed toed shoes are recommended.  Meet the ranger at the Visitor Center at 8am.  This program will be cancelled in the event of a thunderstorm or other inclement weather.</p>\n<p><em>Español: </em></p>\n<p><em>Únase a un guardaparque para una caminata en uno de los senderos cortos cerca del Centro de Visitantes. Aprende sobre la historia, geología, plantas, y animales del monumento. La caminata será en un sendero fácil y bastante plano y la distancia total no superará una milla (1,6 km). </em></p>\n<p><em>¡</em><em>Traiga agua, protector solar, bocadillos, y sus preguntas! Se recomiendan zapatos cerrados. Encuentre al guardaparque frente al Bookcliff View Shelter a las 8:00am. Este programa se cancelará en caso de tormento eléctrica u otras inclemencias del tiempo.  </em></p>",
        "category": "Regular Event",
        "tags": [],
        "location": "",
        "coordinates": {
          "latitude": "39.100868",
          "longitude": "-108.734488"
        },
        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "2025-07-16, 2025-07-17",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      },
      {
        "title": "Evening Program: The History of Dinosaur in 5 Acts",
        "description": "<p>Join a ranger for a 30-45 minute talk at the Green River Campground Program Circle, near Loop B Site 22. Topics vary from geology, history, wildlife, and more. Evening Programs occur on select nights. Programs are designed for general audiences. Bug spray is recommended. Extra parking for non-campers is available in Loop B. </p>\n<p><strong>Planned Topic:</strong> The History of Dinosaur. Discover the history of Dinosaur National Monument.</p>\n<p><em><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Please Note</span>: Program topics may change due to unforeseen schedule changes. Programs may be canceled due to adverse weather, for visitor or employee safety, or because of staffing shortages caused by emergencies such as fire or medical conditions.</em></p>",
        "category": "Regular Event",
        "tags": [
          "ranger",
          "talk",
          "evening",
          "program",
          "campground",
          "green river",
          "ranger talks",
          "evening program",
          "campfire program"
        ],
        "location": "Evening programs are located in the Green River Campground on the Utah side of the park. Talks are given from the Green River Campfire Circle, near Loop B Site 22, across from the restrooms.",
        "coordinates": {
          "latitude": "40.422159",
          "longitude": "-109.243467"
        },
        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "2025-07-16",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      },
      {
        "title": "Night Sky Program",
        "description": "<p>Let rangers introduce you to the night skies above Dinosaur! The evening includes a ranger talk followed by night sky viewing as weather permits. Meet at the plastic benches inside the closed loop at the south end of the Split Mountain Campground. No pets allowed.</p>\n<p>To preseve everyone's darkness-adapted vision, please keep flashlights pointed at the ground. Dark-sky friendly red covers for flashlights will be provided. Parking for non-campers is available at the front of the camprgound.</p>\n<p><em><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Please Note</span>: Programs may be canceled due to adverse weather, for visitor or employee safety, or because of staffing shortages caused by emergencies such as fire or medical conditions.</em></p>",
        "category": "Regular Event",
        "tags": [
          "night sky",
          "ranger talk",
          "program",
          "stargazing",
          "moon talk",
          "sky viewing",
          "telescopes",
          "evening program"
        ],
        "location": "Park in the main lot at the front of the campground and walk to the back. Meet at the plastic benches inside the closed loop at the south end of the Split Mountain Campground.",
        "coordinates": {
          "latitude": "40.438941",
          "longitude": "-109.252462"
        },
        "dateTime": {
          "dates": "2025-07-16",
          "times": "All day"
        },
        "contactInfo": {}
      },
      {
        "title": "Up Close and Personal",
        "description": "<p>Meet a ranger on the back porch of the visitor center to discover more about the monument!  Stop by anytime from 1:30pm to 2:30pm to learn more about the animals, history, and geology of Colorado National Monument with this hands on program.  This program is great for all ages.</p>\n<p>It will be held rain or shine.  In the event of inclement weather, this program moves inside to the exhibit hall.</p>\n<p><em>Español: </em></p>\n<p><em>¡Conoce a un guardaparque en el porche trasero del Centro de Visitantes para descubrir más sobre el monumento! Pase en cualquier momento de las 2 hasta las 3 de la tarde para aprender más sobre los animales, la historia, la geología, o los insectos del Monumento Nacional de Colorado. Este programa es ideal para todas las edades. </em></p>\n<p><em>Se mantendrá lluvia o brillo. En caso de inclemencias del tiempo, este programa se mueve dentro de la sala de exposiciones. </em></p>",
