    {
      "title": "Johnson Farm Guided Exploration (Peaks of Otter - Milepost 86)",
      "description": "<p>Step back in time to the 1920s and 1930s when you visit the Johnson Farm at milepost 86 in the Peaks of Otter area. You can join an optional tour of farmhouse with park staff upon your arrival to the farm. The farm grounds are open for self-guiding no matter when you visit.</p>\n<p>The Johnson Farm represents three generations starting in 1852. The farmhouse was refurbished in the 1970s to its appearance in the 20s and 30s. The farm represents the community in Peaks of Otter before the Blue Ridge Parkway Road.</p>\n<p>The farm is only accessible by hiking a little over 1 mile from the Peaks of Otter Visitor Center at milepost 85.6. Comfortable hiking shoes, water and sunscreen is strongly recommended. The Johnson Farm buildings are subject to close due to weather.</p>",
