      "description": "<p>Join a ranger for a guided phenology walk along the Sundew Trail on the Schoodic Peninsula. Observe the seasonal changes happening around us. Notice the plants budding, blooming, fruiting, and leaf changes that are tied to the time of year. Learn how scientists and citizens use phenology to track climate patterns and the health of ecosystems. Become a citizen scientist by collecting data and recording observations that will be used by national phenology organizations. </p>\n<p><strong>Meet in front of Eliot Hall at the Schoodic Education and Research Center</strong></p>",
