      {
        "title": "Junior Angler Program: Mount Desert Island",
        "description": "<div data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Always wanted to learn how to fish? Don’t have access to a pond or lake near you? Not sure what gear you need to get started? The wait is over! Join a park ranger for a 2-hour program geared towards kids ages 6-15 and fish along the shorelines of Acadia. All children must be accompanied by an adult. The program includes the use of a fishing pole and personal floatation device.  </div>\n<ul>\n<li>All children must have an adult present throughout the 2-hour program. Those 16 and older are not able to fish unless they possess a Maine freshwater fishing license.  </li>\n<li>Participants must wear traction footwear (sneakers, hiking boots, muck boots, etc.). Flip-flops and crocs will not be allowed. </li>\n<li>Make sure participants come with plenty of water, snacks, sunscreen, bug spray, and hat. SPF lightweight clothing is recommended.    </li>\n<li>Location of the program will be given at registration.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><strong><strong>Dates: </strong></strong>all begin at 8:00am\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\">\n<li>\n<div data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Tuesday, July 1</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Wednesday, July 2</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Thursday, July 3</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Saturday, July 5</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Tuesday, July 8</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Wednesday, July 9</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Friday, July 11</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Saturday, July 12</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div><strong>Accessibility:</strong> You may request sign language, live audio description, assistive listening devices, or other accommodation for any scheduled park event or program at Acadia by contacting us at least 10 days in advance at 207-288-8832 or acadia_information@nps.gov. Learn more at https://go.nps.gov/AcadiaAccessibility</div>",
