    {
      "title": "Paddle the Park with Chattahoochee National Park Conservancy",
      "description": "<p><strong>Paddle the Park Series: Garrard Landing to Don White Park</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Friday, June 13th</strong></p>\n<p><strong>9:00 AM launch<em> </em></strong><em>(trip will take approximately 1.5-3 hours including shuttle, and time on the water can vary depending on water levels and how much participants paddle)</em></p>\n<p>Join park Friends' group Chattahoochee National Park Conservancy for a guided paddle series in partnership with Nantahala Outdoor Center (NOC)! Whether you’re a seasoned paddler or brand new to the river, this is your chance to experience the beauty of the Chattahoochee from a whole new perspective. Each trip highlights a different stretch of the river, from peaceful flatwater floats to gentle rapids—all led by expert NOC guides.</p>\n<p>This is a peaceful float through the heart of the river corridor (4.5 miles, flatwater).</p>\n<p><strong>What's Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Kayak or ducky (inflatable kayak), paddle, &amp; life jacket</li>\n<li>Guided trip with NOC experts</li>\n<li>Safety instruction and river interpretation</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"w-full md:w-2/3 md:pl-5\">\n<div class=\"description-content\">\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: This paddle will proceed rain or shine. However, it will be canceled if river flows exceed 5,000 CFS, if E. coli levels are high, or in the event of lightning. Participants will be notified via phone in the event of cancellation.</p>\n<p>This program is in partnership with Nantahala Outdoor Center (NOC) and all participants must complete NOC's waiver prior to program start. Please complete the waiver included in your registration confirmation email. Thank you!</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"w-full md:w-1/6\">\n<div class=\"w-9/10 mx-auto border-t border-gray-300 md:border-t-0 mt-8 md:mb-0 mb-8\"> </div>\n<div class=\"portal-page-location flex flex-col\" data-v-760a1e2c=\"\">\n<div class=\"event-location-name\" data-v-760a1e2c=\"\"> </div>\n</div>\n</div>",
      "category": "Regular Event",
      "tags": [],
      "location": "Gerrard Landing. See event registration link for more information.",
      "coordinates": {
        "latitude": "",
        "longitude": ""
      },
      "dateTime": {
        "dates": "2025-07-11",
        "times": "All day"
      },
      "contactInfo": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Learn to Fish!",
      "description": "<p>Join the National Park Service to learn the basics of fishing, gear, and freshwater fishing in Georgia. We’ll practice casting and get to spend some time fishing in Island Ford pond, while also learning about freshwater fish of Georgia and how to be a responsible angler. Interested participants of any age can also earn a Junior Ranger Angler badge. We will provide fishing gear.</p>\n<p><strong>Location:  </strong>Island Ford Pond at Island Ford, 8800 Roberts Dr, Sandy Springs, GA, 30350. Entrance to the park is at 8800 Roberts Drive. Go to the second parking lot and walk across the road to the pond, or park in front of the Visitor Center and walk ~5 minutes on a forest trail down to the pond.</p>\n<p><strong>Bring</strong>: Please bring water. A hat and sunscreen are recommended. <strong>NOTE: Anyone over the age of 16 must have a valid fishing license to participate in the program, available here:</strong> <a href=\"https://georgia.gov/purchase-fishing-or-hunting-license\">Purchase a Fishing or Hunting License | Georgia.gov</a></p>\n<p><strong>Facilities:  </strong>Restroom and water fountain at Hewlett Lodge Visitor Center</p>",
      "category": "Regular Event",
      "tags": [],
      "location": "Island Ford Pond at Island Ford, 8800 Roberts Dr, Sandy Springs, GA, 30350. Entrance to the park is at 8800 Roberts Drive. Go to the second parking lot and walk across the road to the pond, or park in front of the Visitor Center and walk ~5 minutes on a forest trail down to the pond.",
      "coordinates": {
        "latitude": "",
        "longitude": ""
      },
      "dateTime": {
        "dates": "2025-07-12",
        "times": "All day"
      },
      "contactInfo": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Second Saturday Sweep: Chattahoochee Cleanup Crew with Chattahoochee National Park Conservancy",
      "description": "<p><strong>Join official park Friends group, Chattahoochee National Park Conservancy, for their Second Saturday Sweep: Chattahoochee Community Cleanup! </strong></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Each month, Chattahoochee National Park Conservancy hosts a cleanup at one of the park units along Chattahoochee River National Recreation Area. It is a great way to explore more of the beautiful 66 miles of trails and 48 miles of river the National Park Service protects. Help us protect and preserve the beauty of the Chattahoochee River by participating in this community cleanup effort! We will begin our day by meeting at the trailhead in the parking lot of the Powers Island Unit at 10 AM. We will walk as a group across the bridge to pick up trash along the water and trail of the Powers Island Unit. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>All necessary supplies will be provided, including trash pickers, gloves, and trash bags. This cleanup takes place in a hiking environment, so please wear appropriate clothes and sturdy shoes suitable for outdoor activities.</strong></p>",
      "category": "Regular Event",
      "tags": [],
      "location": "Powers Island Unit. 5450 Interstate N Pkwy\n\nSandy Springs, GA 30328",
      "coordinates": {
        "latitude": "",
        "longitude": ""
      },
      "dateTime": {
        "dates": "2025-07-12",
        "times": "All day"
      },
      "contactInfo": {}
    }
  ],
