    {
      "title": "Discovery Table",
      "description": "<p>Every day, a National Park Service ranger will set up a table with a special topic about the park. At these fun tables, kids can talk to a park ranger, ask questions, and learn new things. You might discover interesting facts about local animals, plants, or the history of the park. Each table is a great way to connect with nature and explore the amazing Mississippi River!</p>\n<p>Discovery tables happen almost every day, depending on the staff available. Be sure to call the Mississippi River Visitor Center to check if they are happening before you visit!</p>",
