    {
      "title": "Ranger-led demonstration: Appalachian Rag Dolls",
      "description": "<div>\n<p><span data-olk-copy-source=\"MailCompose\">Come stitch together a little piece of history at the Crossville Visitor Center!</span></p>\n</div>\n<div>Step back in time to experience the tradition of rag doll making! On Saturday, June 21, join a ranger at the Crossville Visitor Center for a hands-on demonstration celebrating the cherished Appalachian craft. This hands-on demonstration for kids and the young at heart will be available anytime between 11 am and 1 pm (Central Time).</div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>Crossville Visitor Center is located at <span data-teams=\"true\">176 River Otter Drive</span> Crossville, TN. </div>\n<p>Worth 6 GO BIG Points. To learn more about the GO BIG 2025 Challenge, go to <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/biso/planyourvisit/big-south-fork-go-big-challenge.htm\">Big South Fork GO BIG Challenge - Big South Fork National River &amp; Recreation Area (U.S. National Park Service)</a></p>",
