    {
      "title": "View with a Ranger: Honey Creek Overlook",
      "description": "<div class=\"x_elementToProof\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Join us for 'View with the Ranger'<strong> </strong>at the Honey Creek Overlook! Every Sunday in June, between 9 AM and 11 AM ET, a park ranger will be at the overlook to share insights on Big South Fork NRRA. Whether you're curious about the birds, the plants along the trail, or the river below, this is your chance to explore the view with a ranger! </div>\n<div class=\"x_elementToProof\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\"> </div>\n<div class=\"x_elementToProof\" data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">Attendance is worth 5 GO BIG Points. To learn more about the Go Big Challenge, visit <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/biso/planyourvisit/big-south-fork-go-big-challenge.htm\">Big South Fork GO BIG Challenge - Big South Fork National River &amp; Recreation Area (U.S. National Park Service)</a>.</div>",
