      {
        "title": "Junior Ranger Fishing Program at Leatherwood Ford",
        "description": "<p>Big South Fork NRRA is encouraging school-age children to learn to fish with a park ranger.</p>\n<p>A park ranger will introduce school-age children to the fundamentals of fishing, help identify some native fish of the area, and why a river ecosystem is so important. At the end of the program, youth will receive a fishing pole, tackle box, and the official Junior Ranger Angler Badge. <strong>Fishing items are limited to first-time participants only</strong>.</p>\n<p>This program is made possible by a <a href=\"https://www.nationalparks.org/explore/programs/junior-ranger-angler\">Junior Ranger Angler grant</a> from the National Park Foundation.</p>",
