    {
      "title": "Trail to Treasure Walking Tour",
      "description": "<p>Join our knowledgeable rangers and volunteers for a one-hour guided walking tour of Pioneer Square! Learn about Seattle’s foundation and other fascinating history right in the heart of its oldest neighborhood. Hear the powerful stories of how Seattle became the bustling city it is today.</p>\n<p>Tours meet in the park lobby at 11 am. Topics and content will vary slightly by guide. Please note that the tour requires walking through downtown Seattle: walking surfaces will be uneven, traffic and noise are present, and temperatures can be hot. Please plan accordingly.</p>\n<p>If you need accommodations, please contact the front desk prior to the tour. See accommodations available on our Accessibility page: <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/klse/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm\">Accessibility - Klondike Gold Rush - Seattle Unit National Historical Park (U.S. National Park Service)</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>",
