      "title": "Guided Photography Walk: Hurricane Ridge",
      "description": "<p><strong>Photography Walk Program</strong><br /><em>Vital Intersections - Where Science and Art Meet</em></p>\n<p><strong>Join Us for a Special Program with 2025 Artist-in-Residence</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wednesday, July 16 2025, 9:30 am - 11 am<br />Meet at the picnic area pullout just past the Wolf Creek Trailhead on Hurricane Hill Road.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Program Details: </strong>Olympic National Park is excited to welcome acclaimed photographer, poet, and author Jerry Fleury as our 2025 Artist-in-Residence. Known for his evocative storytelling that combines photography, poetry, and place-based narratives, Jerry will spend part of the summer creating new work inspired by the park’s diverse pollinator species and vibrant landscapes.</p>\n<p>Join us for a short walk and a creative photography session, where you will learn hands-on photography techniques from a seasoned artist. Jerry will also share stories from his work in various national parks. Bring your questions and curiosity!</p>\n<p>Whether you're a beginner or an experienced photographer, this is a unique opportunity to explore the natural world through a creative lens.</p>\n<p><strong>What to bring:</strong> Your camera, comfortable shoes, and creative spirit!</p>\n<p><strong>Limited to 10 participants – Registration required (email </strong><a href=\"mailto:olym_volunteer@nps.gov\"><strong>olym_volunteer@nps.gov</strong></a><strong> to register)</strong></p>\n<p><em>Ranger-led programs may be cancelled at any time due to operational priorities and/or safety concerns. For the latest updates and info, inquire with park staff, call 360-565-3130, or visit us online at </em><a href=\"http://www.nps.gov/olym\"><em>www.nps.gov/olym</em></a><em>.</em></p>\n<p><em>For a calendar of park events, including anticipated conditions and expectations at ranger-led programs, visit: </em><a href=\"http://www.nps.gov/olym/planyourvisit/calendar.htm\"><em>www.nps.gov/olym/planyourvisit/calendar.htm</em></a><em>.</em></p>",
