    {
      "title": "One Secret Under Many Roofs: Housing in Oak Ridge During the Manhattan Project [Oak Ridge, TN]",
      "description": "<p>Join a ranger at the public opening of the restored Manhattan Project-Era Flat Top house located on the grounds of the Children's Museum of Oak Ridge. This free program will discuss the many different types of housing found throughout the Secret City during World War II and the steps taken to ensure that a rapidly expanding population had shelter, all while working on a top-secret project. Visitors will also have the opportunity to tour the interior of the Flat Top house for the first time since its restoration.</p>",
      "category": "Regular Event",
