    {
      "title": "Building America's Secret City: Guided Ranger Walk in Jackson Square [Oak Ridge, TN]",
      "description": "<p>Manhattan Project National Historical Park will present a free program in Jackson Square. <br /><br />Jackson Square, or Town Center No. 1, formed the social and economic center of the wartime community of Oak Ridge. Stroll through the townsite to learn how Oak Ridgers created community in the atomic city.<br /><br /> During the walk, rangers and visitors will discuss what it took to shape Oak Ridge during World War II through routines and traditions brought from near and far.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Program ends at the Jackson Square Tennis Courts right on time for the Tennis Court Dance. </p>",
      "category": "Special Event",
      "tags": [],
      "location": "Jackson Square, Oak Ridge, TN\n243 Jackson Square, Oak Ridge, TN 37830\n\nThe program will begin at the fountain in the main parking lot.",
      "coordinates": {
