      {
        "title": "Ranger Program",
        "description": "<p>Join our knowledgeable rangers and volunteers for a program on various topics surrounding the Klondike Gold Rush, Seattle, and the Pacific Northwest!</p>\n<p>Programs begin at 11:30 AM. Check-in at or call the Visitor Center front desk for the topic and location in the museum. Topics and content will vary by ranger. </p>\n<p>Topics include: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gold Panning</li>\n<li>Women of the Klondike</li>\n<li>Gold, Minerals, &amp; More!</li>\n<li>Immigrants to the Klondike</li>\n<li>Photographers of the Klondike</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you need accommodations, please contact the front desk prior to the tour. See accommodations available on our Accessibility page: <a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/klse/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm\">Accessibility - Klondike Gold Rush - Seattle Unit National Historical Park (U.S. National Park Service)</a>.</p>",
